  "rationale": "store_preserves_bindings quantifies over arbitrary successful store calls and concludes equality of the whole binding list. Its hypothesis is precisely store classes before place ty = some after. The theorem makes no runtime safety, view equality or termination claim. The linked store definition introduces its operation. Rooted-foundation review: the structural invariants now require explicit rootedness (including pending values) plus unique/compatible ownership. Allocation bounds remain solely for freshness; no safety proof assumes edge-age order or global DAG structure. Changed proof selections retain their public statement unless this unit explicitly defines the revised invariant or example. Given/Shared root transport and path reasoning were reviewed by their implementing agents, with fresh review of root-owned unpacking, GC, frame rerooting, class retention and the refill example. Earlier syntax and runtime rules are unchanged. The widened invariant domain is covered by recompilation of all earlier safety proofs and concrete shared-cycle/nonmonotonic-ID regressions, not by a claim that constructors can generate cycles.",
